package Physics.Tests

use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D

/*
A box under the triangle is pushed down, since the collider treats the
triangle as two sided.

Unless a test says otherwise, the triangle is a large one lying flat
at height 0, from MakeLargeTriangle, with the usual margin of 0.04, so
its thickened surface is at 0.04. The box is 0.5 on each side for
collisions (see RunBox), with no rotation, and the triangle is item A.
A box whose center is at 0.28 has its bottom at 0.03, so it sinks 0.01
into the surface.
*/
class BoxTriangleUnderneathTest is PhysicsTest
    on create
        SetName("Box and triangle: underneath")
    end

    action Run
        LocalCollisionPoints3D points = RunBox(MakeLargeTriangle(0.04), MakeTransform(0, -0.28, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0), false)
        CheckWhole("box underneath: four contacts", points:GetPointCount(), 4)
        CheckAllContacts("box underneath", points, 0, 1, 0, -0.01)
        CheckWhole("box underneath: corner", CountContactsNear(points, 0.25, -0.03, 0.25), 1)
    end
end
